    "notes": "1. 'total_operating_cost' includes all operating expenses that reduce gross margin to arrive at operating profit. This includes Cost of sales, Marketing and selling expenses, General and administrative expenses, and Other operating income and expenses (which is a net expense). 'Income/(Loss) from joint ventures and associates' is not included as it is a separate line item before operating profit and is not a cost. 2. 'interest_expenses' includes 'Cost of net financial debt' and 'Interest on lease liabilities' as they are explicit interest costs. 'Other financial income and expenses' is excluded as it is a net figure containing non-interest items (e.g., dividends, FX, fair value adjustments). 3. All values are taken directly from the primary statement. Numbers in parentheses are treated as positive values for cost/expense fields per rule 13. 4. The scale is 1E6 (millions) as stated in the statement. 5. Supplementary tables provide detail but are not used for the core consolidated values, except to confirm the composition of line items.",
